Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:03:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Phase 2: exit-policy (trailing-stop / take-profit)
 research backtest

Phase 1 gave AURA a full discovered coin universe and a second, mirrored
entry candidate (both purely at the .13 recognition/reporting level --
direction is decided nowhere there). aura_regime_backtest_v2.py separately
asks whether the frozen entry candidate has an edge over a random-time
baseline, using a *fixed* forward-return horizon. Neither answers the next
question in the agreed 5-phase plan: once a trade is open, when should it
actually exit?

aura_exit_policy_backtest.py adds that research, scoped and designed per
Martin's explicit answers to this session's clarifying questions:

- Direction (simulation-only, does not touch any live file): FROZEN_CANDIDATE
  ("BEAR x LOW ATR x POSITIVE bar-2") simulated as a LONG entry,
  MIRROR_CANDIDATE ("BULL_OR_NEUTRAL x LOW x NON_POSITIVE") simulated as a
  SHORT entry. .23's VALIDATED_LONG_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS /
  VALIDATED_SHORT_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS remain frozenset(), untouched --
  verified directly by a test that imports .23 and asserts both stay empty.
- Scope: full discovered Alpaca crypto universe by default (not the
  narrower shortlist v2 defaults to). Every result row is labeled
  validated_entry=True/False (True only for BTC/USD, ETH/USD, the only
  symbols with a separately-validated entry signal so far) and the report
  is split into two segments so an unvalidated-entry symbol's exit-policy
  result is never read as equivalent to a BTC/ETH one.
- Parameter grid (my proposal, Martin approved): trailing stops at
  1/2/3/5%, take-profits at 2/4/6/10%, plus a trail-only variant per
  trailing-stop level -- all overridable via --trailing-stops/--take-profits.
- Full statistical rigor, matching v2 exactly but applied to policy choice
  instead of ATR-threshold choice: TRAIN/TEST split (70/30), the policy
  grid is searched on TRAIN only (never on TEST), the chosen policy is
  evaluated out-of-sample on TEST, a block bootstrap reports a CI and
  P(mean>0) on TEST trade returns, and an expanding-window walk-forward
  (v2's own block_boundaries) re-runs the same TRAIN-only search per fold
  to check the result isn't an artifact of the single 70/30 split.

Implementation notes:
- Reuses aura_regime_backtest_v2.py directly (loaded via importlib, this
  repo's existing convention for cross-file reuse) for its exact indicator
  computation (compute_regime_series, itself built on .12's
  wilder_atr/build_4h), data fetch, bootstrap_mean_ci, and
  block_boundaries/slice_by_range -- none of that is reimplemented.
  MIRROR_CANDIDATE's entry condition is the literal complement of FROZEN's
  (trend/bar2), same single global ATR threshold, verified against .12's
  own regime_state construction (trend_bear / bar2_positive / atr14_pct).
- Trade simulation walks 1H bars forward from just after entry with no
  look-ahead: each bar's stop/target check uses the running favorable
  extreme as of the END of the prior bar; the extreme is only updated with
  the current bar's own high/low after that bar has been checked. A same-
  bar stop+target collision resolves to the stop (conservative), matching
  this repo's older stock exit-policy research convention. A trade open
  past --max-hold-hours (default 240h) closes TIMEOUT at the last bar's
  close -- a research safety cap, not a live-position claim; TIMEOUT rate
  is reported per policy.
- Baseline for the "does active exit management help" comparison: the same
  TEST entries' plain 24h-hold net return (v2's own fwd_24h column) --
  excess over this baseline is what's reported, not just "is it positive".
- Fails closed (exit 2) before any network call when Alpaca credentials are
  missing, same as v2.
- Also gitignores research/exit_policy_backtest/ (this script's output)
  and research/regime_backtest_v2/ (v2's output -- was missing from
  .gitignore, which is why it showed up as untracked-file noise earlier
  this session; fixed alongside since it's the same class of entry).

Research only. Never places an order, never touches live/paper execution,
never reads or writes anything under .19/.22/.23's live execution path.

Added tests/test_aura_exit_policy_backtest.py (25 tests): LONG and SHORT
trailing-stop hits, fixed take-profit hits, same-bar stop+target collision
resolving to stop (both directions), no-look-ahead verification (a bar's
own high cannot trigger its own stop), TIMEOUT, NO_DATA_AFTER_ENTRY, cost
subtracted from net not gross, FROZEN vs MIRROR entry-condition correctness
including new-episode-after-gap detection, an unknown-candidate ValueError,
trade_summary statistics (win rate, profit factor, timeout rate, empty
input), the policy grid's trail-only variants, search_best_policy's
train-only selection and minimum-trade-count gate, the direction mapping
and candidate-label sync with .13's live constants, a direct assertion that
.23's live allowlists stay empty, and the credentials fail-closed CLI path.
Also verified end-to-end against a longer synthetic random-walk series
(1200 synthetic 1H bars): runs with no exceptions and correctly reports
NOT_PROMISING/INSUFFICIENT_DATA on pure noise -- no spurious PROMISING.

Full suite: 113 passed (pytest, excluding the two Alpaca-credential tests
that fail in this sandbox for unrelated reasons).

This is Phase 2 of the agreed 5-phase plan, authorized by Martin's "Please
do" after reviewing and answering this session's clarifying questions on
direction, symbol scope, parameter grid, and statistical rigor.

